    "intro_html":  "A shepherd\u0027s pie is a filling under a mashed potato roof, and once you understand that, the filling is up for negotiation. This one uses slow cooked pulled pork in a tomato and balsamic gravy with carrots, peas and corn, all of it under a layer of mashed potatoes with cream and butter worked in. It bakes until the top browns in ridges. Of everything in this section, this is the dish that reheats closest to the way it came out of the oven.",
